{
  "case_id": "2019-19-715",
  "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Patrick Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STRAWBRIDGE: Before these cases -- Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The subpoenas at issue here are unprecedented in every sense. Before these cases, no court had ever upheld the use of Congress's subpoena power to demand the personal records of a sitting President, and no committee of Congress had even tried to compel production of such a broad swath of the President's personal papers, let alone for the stated purpose of considering potential legislation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For several reasons, Justice Gorsuch. To begin, the subpoena power is an implied power, and this Court made clear, most recently in NFIB v. Sebelius, that Congress cannot use its implied powers to challenge the structure of government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is this subpoena not provide -- supported by a substantial legislative need?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These cases are truly historic. Three different congressional committees have targeted not the official records of the President but his personal records, stretching back years before he was even a candidate for office. The potential to harass and undermine the President and the presidency is plain. It's not much to ask that before the House delves into the President's personal life, it explain in some meaningful way what laws it is considering and why it needs the President's documents in particular."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Which is, until Congress investigates, A, it doesn't have a chance to determine what might be valid, and, B, we don't have a chance then to look at an actual law and say it may or may not be valid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- Mr. Wall, in what other setting does any investigative body have to do more than what was done here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Wall, I'd like to go back to your use of Clinton v. Jones because I -- I had read that case differently."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, harassing and undermining the President -- I mean, the point of some of those suits is presumably to harass and undermine the President, and the Court let them go, let -- you know, let them proceed. And it said the only thing we're going to be concerned about is if you come in to us and say, in defending those suits, you're going to be prevented from performing the responsibilities that we, the nation, need you to perform. Are you making an argument of that kind?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: All right. Well, there might be congress -- there might be constitutionally based privileges. Which constitutionally based privileges apply to a subpoena for records in the hands of a third-party?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0003-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "President Trump's personal records and his businesses and his family have been heavily involved in those very activities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Good morning, Mr. Letter. In -- in -- in talking to the Chief Justice about the limits on congressional power, you said -- and tell me if I'm quoting you correctly -- you said that a subpoena couldn't impair the President in carrying out his constitutional functions. Is that -- is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Letter",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There has been no claim of privilege here. There has been no claim that there is a burden. No claim whatsoever. So those may be relevant in different cases, but certainly not this one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress were to subpoena personal records in the hands of a third-party regarding a member of the other House, let's say someone in a leadership position in the other House, do you think that the doctrine of separation of powers would impose any limitation on that subpoena?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Patrick Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "91c0b544df5566ac5f3a98e133ae7e598aef0753b4751fbdd5b1830109360769",
      "evidence_id": "ev-91c0b544df55-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no reason under his theory why the President and his family and his grandchildren could not be declared useful case studies and, therefore, Congress could send out a subpoena for their medical records."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-19-715",
      "confidence": 0.0,
